    "mission_1.compare.arc": "The robot rotated only 0.8720 rad instead of 1.60 rad and traveled 0.316m instead of 0.6m. The robot's timer could have stopped; the safety node could have reduced the velocity.",
    "mission_1.compare.straight": "It's a difference of -0.1720 from the predicted path travel. I predict 3 causes, the robot slips on the surface, the robot doesn't travel at the commanded speed, and lastly, the robot doesn't travel the commanded time.",
    "mission_1.compare.turn_then_drive": "The robot only turned 0.7630 rad instead of my predicted 3.14 rad, which causes the final position to be different. A causes could be that the turning command stopped too early.",
    "mission_1.error.arc": "",
    "mission_1.error.straight": "",
    "mission_1.error.turn_then_drive": "",
    "mission_1.hallway_analysis": "Sudden turns or abrupt straight driving could scare pedestrians because the robot's path to an outsider isn't obvious. Lowering the turn rate will make the motion smoother and more predictable. Downside being a maneuver will take longer. We can use lidar to track and detect people and objects to limit speed when close to things or people for safety, then ramp it up when clear.",
